From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 14:56:33 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 293/342] realtekwifi: the receive watchdog only watches a link
 that is up

The previous commit left out the time after a scan: the radio waits on one channel
for the supplicant's choice, and silence there still counted. One cold boot took
147 s to get an address, through restarts. Without a link, or during a scan, the
2 minute limit applies.

Cold boots are steady now: an address 48-51 s after power-on, 10 of 10, with no
restart. They all choose 2.4 GHz though. The restarts had been what brought 5 of 8
to 5 GHz.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../network/wlan/realtekwifi/dev/rtwn/if_rtwn.c    | 14 +++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/network/wlan/realtekwifi/dev/rtwn/if_rtwn.c b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/network/wlan/realtekwifi/dev/rtwn/if_rtwn.c
index b25e669f2d..159f3993ef 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/network/wlan/realtekwifi/dev/rtwn/if_rtwn.c
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/network/wlan/realtekwifi/dev/rtwn/if_rtwn.c
@@ -1479,18 +1479,22 @@ rtwn_watchdog(void *arg)
 	/*
 	 * A chip that has stopped receiving (see rx_silence_limit): after frames
 	 * came and then none for the limit, or every 2 minutes if a restart
-	 * didn't bring any, as there may simply be nothing around.  A scan spends
-	 * seconds on empty channels, and a restart would only start it again:
-	 * the 2 minutes there too.
+	 * didn't bring any, as there may simply be nothing around.  Only a link
+	 * that is up has frames to expect: a scan spends seconds on empty
+	 * channels, the radio waits on one for the supplicant's choice after it,
+	 * and a restart would only start all that again.  The 2 minutes there too.
 	 */
 	if (sc->rx_silence_limit != 0) {
+		struct ieee80211vap *vap = TAILQ_FIRST(&ic->ic_vaps);
+		int linked = vap != NULL && vap->iv_state == IEEE80211_S_RUN &&
+		    (ic->ic_flags & IEEE80211_F_SCAN) == 0;
+
 		if (sc->sc_rx_transfers != sc->sc_rx_seen) {
 			sc->sc_rx_seen = sc->sc_rx_transfers;
 			sc->sc_rx_silence = 0;
 			sc->sc_rx_flowing = 1;
 		} else if (++sc->sc_rx_silence
-		    >= (sc->sc_rx_flowing && (ic->ic_flags & IEEE80211_F_SCAN) == 0 ?
-		    sc->rx_silence_limit : 120)) {
+		    >= (sc->sc_rx_flowing && linked ? sc->rx_silence_limit : 120)) {
 			ic_printf(ic, "nothing received for %d s, restarting\n",
 			    sc->sc_rx_silence);
 			sc->sc_rx_silence = 0;
